an Kotleba", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "kotlebists-peoples-party-our-slovakia", "targetName": "Kotlebists – People's Party Our Slovakia", "context": "Marian Kotleba's leadership has been pivotal in the success and visibility of the Kotlebists."}], "places": [{"name": "Banská Bystrica, Slovakia", "role": "Headquarters"}, {"name": "Bratislava, Slovakia", "role": "Political Center"}, {"name": "Košice, Slovakia", "role": "Electoral Base"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Kotlebists – People's Party Our Slovakia", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "kotlebists-peoples-party-our-slovakia"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2532168", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People%27s_Party_Our_Slovakia"], "tags": ["Slovakia", "political party", "Europe", "Political Parties & Organizations", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Kotlebists – People's Party Our Slovakia contributed to the historical record of the Contemporary period. Key lasting impacts include: Shaped institutional landscape and community development. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "The Kotlebists have significantly influenced Slovak political discourse, challenging traditional parties and reshaping public perceptions of nationalism and immigration. Their electoral successes indicate a shift towards right-wing populism in Eastern Europe, with implications for future governance and societal cohesion.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-26T20:51:45Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30219781560", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Far-right slovak political party Headquartered in Banská Bystrica. Founded 2009.", "newValue": "The Kotlebists – People's Party Our Slovakia (ĽSNS) emerged in the context of a growing far-right movement in Slovakia, officially founded in 2009 by Marian Kotleba. The party is headquartered in Banská Bystrica and has its roots in the political and social discontent stemming from the global financial crisis of 2008, which exacerbated nationalistic and anti-establishment sentiments in Eastern Europe. The party's ideology is characterized by Slovak nationalism, social conservatism, and a strong anti-immigrant stance, positioning it within a broader European trend of rising right-wing populism.

